{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And to those who keep My commandments</b> is juxtaposed to <b>You shall not take [the name]</b> — for even in the observance of commandments there is an aspect of <b>you shall not take</b>, for one who performs a commandment not for its own sake is as if he takes the name of Heaven in vain. Alternatively, a warning not to transgress <b>you shall not take</b> in the matter of observing a commandment, for one swears to fulfill the commandment."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:52.102493749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}